<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<resources>
    <!--
      The platform theme, which matters for exactly one frame: the one the system draws before
      Compose has drawn anything.

      This inherited android:Theme.Material.Light.NoActionBar once - a LIGHT parent under
      an app that is now dark on every screen. Measured on an API 37 device rather than assumed: the
      decor view's background was #FAFAFA, so every cold start painted a white window and then
      replaced it with #15120C as soon as Compose caught up. Nobody specified that flash; it was
      left over from a project that had no theme at all.

      windowBackground is set explicitly rather than inherited, because the value has to be the
      same #15120C the Compose theme uses and inheriting a platform grey would put it one platform
      release away from drifting. WindowBackgroundInstrumentedTest resolves this attribute against
      the real theme and fails if it is not the design's background.

      windowLightStatusBar is false so the clock and the battery are drawn light. There is nothing
      here setting statusBarColor or navigationBarColor: from API 35 Android enforces edge-to-edge
      and ignores both, and minSdk is 34 - dead config that reads like a decision is worse than no
      config.
    -->
    <style name="Theme.AgtermRemote" parent="android:Theme.Material.NoActionBar">
        <item name="android:windowBackground">@color/window_background</item>
        <item name="android:windowLightStatusBar">false</item>
        <item name="android:windowLightNavigationBar">false</item>
    </style>
</resources>
